8b8eedff1370c0a34f15c59c6ad91a7896679f","event_uuid":"5dcccc90-aba3-466d-8508-84c538d917aa","position":{"commit_sha":"2f63e298138790cb60140395ffa5421b4b3a57bc","position":"1787291364519298001-5dcccc90-aba3-466d-8508-84c538d917aa"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bcff3408245c8a4f5ae0bd8e8326dea0cca439bf65d5d827cbcb6db15152c4e4","event_uuid":"d130adee-96a1-4484-b5be-3f9c04cb7ac4","position":{"commit_sha":"05b7b963ea4cbcd385a39a86b49c97fe6e1886a3","position":"1787291513011281001-d130adee-96a1-4484-b5be-3f9c04cb7ac4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c94950819a77325e69e1be93f560c38caed609a9bcc5ccde30508e3f840e9d1c","event_uuid":"cdae6588-588a-4b37-a10f-606faf1232c7","position":{"commit_sha":"c819f3e1e998676e84480c5a2b6efa2437fbe155","position":"1787293038963115001-cdae6588-588a-4b37-a10f-606faf1232c7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Created and linked audit task minimum-rainy-fawn. Declared no repository file impact because this phase produces only a proposal. The operator clarified that code-review protocol was outside scope, so the survey now follows the supplied documentation taxonomy with agent-coordination only. The first plan review returned BLOCK because the standards source was not durable in the ticket. Revised the description to preserve the full standards baseline, cite docs/maintenance-audit-runbook.md, explain the shard rationale, and separate acceptance criteria. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787285767566604001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"The second plan review returned BLOCK because docs/maintenance-audit-runbook.md defines perspective shards for code health, not repository-surface shards for documentation. Read the runbook and repository file census. Revised minimum-rainy-fawn to use the runbook only for its exploration-then-refutation sequence. Added three explicit content shards with precedence rules, assigned tracker writes to the root agent, documented excluded artifact classes, and specified the final punctuation pattern set. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787286140940977001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"The third plan review returned PASS with a signed attestation. It advised that the colon scan needs manual classification because structural labels and list introductions are permitted. Claimed minimum-rainy-fawn as joeoakhart@navapbc.com. Repository survey work may now begin. The root agent retains exclusive tracker write ownership.","timestamp":1787286449776370001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Started the master coverage inventory. The repository has 3,222 tracked files. Relevant groups include 10 root documents, 65 top-level docs pages, 103 ADR files, 164 experiment assets, 14 infrastructure documents, 18 example or template documents, 55 CLI help files, 3 packaged guides, 87 reviewer prompts, 40 evaluation or workflow text assets, 555 source Python files, 66 script files, 1,511 test Python files, 91 workflow or configuration files, and 156 machine-corpus assets. A candidate scan across 427 Markdown, RST, or help text files found 7,973 em dash matches across 361 files, 219 en dash matches across 83 files, 216 spaced-hyphen matches across 54 files, 5,121 semicolon matches across 387 files, 1,886 filler-term matches across 292 files, and hard-wrap candidates across 362 Markdown files. These counts include code examples, quotations, technical tokens, and permitted contexts. They are triage signals rather than confirmed defects. Three exploration agents are inspecting the defined shards. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787286632627289001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Survey checkpoint. External documentation and shipped help inspection has produced seventeen evidence-backed draft proposals. Confirmed critical accuracy defects cover DSSE signing and close behavior, import idempotency and batching, Jira project configuration, GitHub Actions identity setup, and adoption templates. Confirmed completeness defects cover omitted create and transition options, truncated MCP summaries, and missing relation or close guidance. Audience defects affect README.md, docs/user-guide.md, docs/config.md, docs/jira-sync-setup.md, docs/exit-codes.md, and packaged plan guidance. The remaining local survey covers authentication, S3, integration guides, package metadata, examples, workflow editor strings, demos, and generated provenance. Three exploration agents continue their assigned read-only shards. The packaged code-review guide will be inspected only as shipped documentation. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787286985418408001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root validation reviewed the prior documentation epic tsunamic-wax-hog and the current documentation gates. That epic already repaired the README quickstart, completed the docs index, generated the CLI and MCP references, and added drift checks. Those completed items will not be proposed again unless current evidence shows a new defect. Current gates cover ADR numbering and indexing, environment registry drift, docs index completeness and relative links, README quickstart execution, generated CLI and MCP references, DCO identity, criteria vocabulary, conflict markers, file size, and selected contract tests. They do not enforce the operator prose constraints or documentation taxonomy. The comment hygiene guard scans only Python comments and docstrings in src, tests, and scripts for rot-prone historical tokens. It does not assess necessity, duplication, formal diction, paragraph shape, or non-Python surfaces. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787287131115901001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Shard C completed its read-only survey of developer comments and embedded prose. It returned eleven candidate remediations. Confirmed P0 findings are the narrow scope and permissive citation exception in scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py, plus stale Jira backend and prompt count documentation. Confirmed P1 groups cover source comments and docstrings, executable prompts and schemas, diagnostics, public library docstrings, infrastructure comments, and diction. P2 groups cover test prose, experiment documentation, and redundant separators. The shard assigned client-facing presentation strings to shard B. It excluded generated evidence, external captures, wording fixtures, code syntax, technical identifiers, and necessary safety rationale from mechanical rewriting. The worktree remained clean.","timestamp":1787287637050745001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root sampling confirmed audience leakage in the client front door. README.md combines onboarding with lock implementation, CI rationale, dependency design, gate internals, development tooling, and repeated install guidance. docs/user-guide.md includes top-level router mechanics and a dated credential incident. Current rebar help omits the intercepted explain, review-plan, review-code, verify-completion, scan-spec, and workflow commands even though the generated CLI reference lists them. Open RP-05 tickets already plan the registry cutover, so the audit will record coordination and post-cutover verification instead of duplicating that implementation. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787287798158239001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root validation found a current signing documentation drift cluster. The public sign help still calls the operation HMAC signing. README.md, docs/manifest-signing.md, docs/event-schema.md, docs/reuse-surface.md, docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md, docs/plan-review-gate.md, docs/llm-framework.md, and docs/sample-ticket-log.jsonl also describe HMAC operation certificates as current. The sign result schema and current implementation state that sign_manifest emits asymmetric sshsig operation certificates. Legacy HMAC utilities remain only for compatibility or non-operation-certificate consumers. This correction requires one coordinated source and generated-help sweep rather than isolated wording changes. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787288139277314001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Survey checkpoint. Root validation confirmed that new manifest writes use DSSE operation certificates with SSHSIG. Legacy HMAC material remains only for limited compatibility paths, while fourteen maintained documentation surfaces still describe HMAC as the current gate mechanism. Import help still promises duplicate creation and future batching even though cold-stall-chalk delivered source-id idempotency, deferred push, chunked commits, and crash resumption. Workflow validation confirmed that JIRA_PROJECT is required by the bridge runner but omitted from workflow preflight. The identity setup guide incorrectly rejects GITHUB_ENV even though four shipped workflows use it for later steps. The first-change guide contradicts make hooks, the Gerrit-only landing path, and the policy against retrying unproven flakes. The docs index also classifies completed plans, handoffs, and validation transcripts as durable documentation even though the supplied taxonomy assigns that history to tickets. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787288300850454001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Shard C completed its read-only survey of developer comments and embedded prose. It returned twelve candidate groups with exact source anchors and false-positive controls.\\n\\n- P0. Replace the narrow Python-only comment hygiene policy. The current checker scans Python files under source, tests, and scripts. It permits a historical block when the block contains a ticket or ADR citation. Extend format-aware enforcement to maintained comments, docstrings, presentation strings, prompts, schemas, evaluation specifications, workflow prose, configuration, Terraform, and shell while excluding syntax, vendored content, generated artifacts, frozen evidence, and technical identifiers.\\n- P0. Correct reconciler prose that still says only the Jira Cloud backend exists, describes Jira Data Center as future work, or presents implemented ACLI and ADF behavior as pending. Current registry decorators, imports, codecs, and Data Center call sites prove both backends and the shared sanitizer contracts.\\n- P1. Rewrite production comments and docstrings around current behavior, nonobvious constraints, ownership, ordering, safety, and failure semantics. Move module-split history, bug chronology, and former paths to the cited tickets or ADRs.\\n- P1. Remove the stale claim that the reviewer prompt hygiene test covers 41 prompts. Its current executable glob resolves 58 files. Derive the count or document the invariant without a fixed number.\\n- P1. Normalize executable prompts, plan-review routing data, evaluation specifications, and schema descriptions without changing criteria meaning, labels, contracts, or scoring intent. Change generated artifacts through their canonical sources.\\n- P1. Rewrite diagnostics, logs, workflow annotations, shell output, and demonstration strings while preserving structured markers, error codes, field names, and compatibility text.\\n- P1. Add missing client API docstrings for unlink, tag, untag, archive, and compact. Document parameters, returns, mutation behavior, error mapping, repo_root, and relation behavior from current wrappers and tests.\\n- P1. Reduce workflow, infrastructure, and configuration comments to current operational rationale. Move measurements, rollout history, former values, and incident narratives to existing tickets. Keep necessary timeout, safety, ordering, secret-handling, and recovery constraints.\\n- P1. Apply contextual diction remediation across canonical prose sources. Replace filler with the mechanism, source, timing, failure mode, or execution boundary. Do not rewrite identifiers or defined domain terms.\\n- P2. Rewrite test comments around the protected invariant and failure oracle. Preserve fixture wording when the wording is under test.\\n- P2. Separate experiment procedure from outcomes. Keep harness docstrings focused on purpose, inputs, outputs, safety, and reproduction. Preserve immutable evidence with provenance and store conclusions in tickets or ADRs.\\n- P2. Remove ornamental dividers and comments that restate adjacent code only after contextual review. Retain semantic navigation labels and nonobvious rationale.\\n\\nMeasured triage signals include 87 reviewer prompts with 791 em dash candidates and 463 semicolon candidates, 31 evaluation specifications with 263 em dash candidates and 208 semicolon candidates, 62 of 102 schemas with connector candidates in 193 descriptive fields, more than 140 exception messages, 215 logging messages, more than 58 print messages, 4,796 separator candidates, and 633 diction candidates. Counts are not defect totals. Syntax, serialized fixtures, external captures, model outputs, generated files, and technical identifiers require exclusion or source-aware handling. Client-facing argparse help, MCP descriptions, package metadata, scaffold text, and issue templates remain assigned to Shard B. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787288511587498001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root verification confirmed two shard C accuracy findings. The reconciler configuration comment names only the jira backend, while registry decorators define both jira and jira-datacenter. The public exports unlink, tag, untag, archive, and compact have no function docstrings in src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py. These findings remain candidates for the complete challenge pass.","timestamp":1787288769710806001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Consolidation checkpoint. The proposal schema has one item identifier, priority, evidence, defect, accuracy basis, target type, audience, action, destination, historical references, and adjudication. The final list will distinguish repository-wide policy, client documentation, shipped help, internal current-state documentation, ADR records, ticket history, comments, embedded prose, and generated artifacts. Cross-surface corrections will remain coordinated batches when one behavior controls every source. Mechanical counts remain triage signals. Quoted third-party text, frozen evidence, technical identifiers, code syntax, serialized fixtures, and generated outputs are excluded from direct rewriting unless their canonical source is maintained. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787288963215102001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Cross-shard validation checkpoint.\\n\\n- The sign result schema and the HMAC removal migration state that sign_manifest emits only asymmetric sshsig operation certificates for the plan-review and completion-verifier kinds. README.md, docs/manifest-signing.md, docs/event-schema.md, docs/reuse-surface.md, docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md, docs/plan-review-gate.md, docs/llm-framework.md, docs/sample-ticket-log.jsonl, src/rebar/_cli/help/sign.txt, and the generated CLI reference still describe current HMAC signing. Legacy HMAC utilities remain for compatibility outside those operation-certificate kinds.\\n- README.md documents six relations, omits caused_by, and says unlink accepts no relation. docs/ticket-model.md and src/rebar/_cli/help/unlink.txt document seven relations and an optional relation selector.\\n- templates/rebar-usage.md, templates/AGENTS.md, and docs/assets/rebar-demo.svg tell clients to claim with an explicit bare assignee. This conflicts with the configured-default policy and Jira-resolvable identity requirements. The templates omit caused_by, and the SVG uses deprecated four-digit ticket references.\\n- src/rebar/_cli/help/import.txt and the generated CLI reference say import always creates duplicates on rerun. src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py implements source_id based idempotent resume and chunked commits for independent passes.\\n- scripts/jira-onboarding-reference/README.md describes onboarding as planned and unavailable although rebar bridge setup is the canonical implemented command.\\n- Both scripts under scripts/jira-pressure-test default REBAR_TICKET_CLI to the deleted src/rebar/_engine/rebar path. Their README therefore promises commands that do not run from a current checkout.\\n- infra/terraform/modules/sso-gate/README.md points to missing infra/shared/auth/RUNBOOK.md. The maintained authentication runbook is infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md.\\n- infra/runbooks/two-vote-gate-rollback.md says the Verified submit requirement ships inactive. infra/gerrit/project.config records the active requirement and omits the disabling applicableIf line.\\n- infra/runbooks/github-mirror-lock.md instructs operators to disable GitHub Issues and GitHub Actions. SUPPORT.md names Issues as the primary support channel, and the repository uses Actions for the Verified gate.\\n- pyproject.toml distributes only LICENSE through license-files. The packaged alias wordlist cites an MIT text under docs/licenses that is not included through that field. NOTICE contains only the optional Pandoc entry. The legacy packaged ticket-wordlist.txt contains no provenance header.\\n- tests/external/live_jira_dc/Dockerfile identifies its upstream path but does not pin an upstream revision or state the upstream license.\\n- examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md lacks the name field that examples/agent-skills/README.md declares mandatory.\\n- docs/concurrency.md and docs/event-schema.md still name deleted shell writers. docs/architecture.md includes pending ADR designs and module-split history. docs/oss-comparison-and-remediation.md and docs/remediation-implementation-plan.md claim that implemented clocks, identity, tag deltas, search predicates, import, export, and Python writers are absent.\\n- ADR 0042 and ADR 0090 contain supersession notices but retain Accepted status. The ADR set lacks consistent metadata. The current ADR-number checker validates numbering and links only.\\n- docs/maintenance-audit-runbook.md describes an 800-line soft cap, dated tool availability, and dated baseline measurements. The project policy now defines an absolute cap.\\n- No project file changed.","timestamp":1787289077255426001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Candidate register checkpoint. Current groups include policy and automated validation, client front-door reduction, signing corrections, import guidance, CLI coverage, MCP summary and manifest checks, adoption assets, user guidance, configuration, identity setup, Jira workflows, contributor workflow, ChatGPT import, architecture, event schema, concurrency, ADR status and links, historical document relocation, exit-code history, API docstrings, source comments, prompts and schemas, diagnostics, workflow comments, tests, and experiments. Each group remains provisional until the filtering pass. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787289610577838001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Accuracy validation added five implementation-backed corrections.\n\n- Jira project configuration is required by src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py, runtime.py, and src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py. docs/config.md, docs/jira-sync-setup.md, bridge-probe help, and generated CLI help still describe a DIG fallback or call JIRA_PROJECT optional.\n- docs/identity-setup.md rejects GITHUB_ENV as an unreliable cross-step channel. Four maintained workflows use GITHUB_ENV for REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY, and additional workflows use it for other later-step values.\n- docs/README.md still describes six ticket relations and files completed plans, handoffs, migration records, and validation transcripts as repository documentation. The current model has seven relations. The supplied taxonomy assigns work history to tickets and reserves internal documentation for current state.\n- pyproject.toml includes only LICENSE in license-files. The bundled alias wordlist cites docs/licenses/adjective-adjective-animal-LICENSE.txt, so distribution metadata and NOTICE need a complete third-party provenance and packaging review.\n- ADR 0042 and ADR 0090 declare Accepted after an explicit supersession notice. scripts/check_adr_numbers.py validates numbering, markers, and links but does not validate lifecycle metadata or relationship consistency.\n\nNo project files changed.","timestamp":1787289724930354001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Draft candidate register before the challenge pass.\\n\\n- D01. Add one canonical repository writing policy that defines ticket, ADR, internal documentation, external documentation, shipped help, comment, generated artifact, and evidence-corpus ownership.\\n- D02. Replace the Python-only comment guard with format-aware prose and paragraph checks across maintained textual surfaces. Preserve explicit exclusions for syntax, technical identifiers, generated outputs, third-party texts, and frozen evidence.\\n- D03. Perform a source-aware cleanup of maintained prose after the policy gate exists. Rewrite prohibited connectors, filler, authenticity padding, contractions, casual diction, and hard-wrapped Markdown through each canonical source.\\n- D04. Reduce README.md to installation, first use, product concepts, supported interfaces, and links. Move contributor process, implementation detail, gate internals, and architecture to their internal homes.\\n- D05. Separate client guidance from implementation and incident history in docs/user-guide.md, docs/config.md, docs/jira-sync-setup.md, docs/exit-codes.md, authentication guides, S3 guidance, and integration guides.\\n- D06. Correct the operation-certificate documentation set from current HMAC claims to the DSSE envelope and sshsig implementation. Preserve legacy HMAC text only where compatibility code still accepts it.\\n- D07. Correct ticket-model guidance across README.md, templates, demos, help, and examples. Document seven relations, optional relation selection for unlink, configured claim defaults, Jira-resolvable explicit assignees, and supported ticket identifier forms.\\n- D08. Correct import help and generated reference text to describe source_id idempotency, crash resumption, deferred push, and chunk-level commit behavior from src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py.\\n- D09. Correct missing or incomplete CLI option and close guidance through canonical help sources. Coordinate generated reference and top-level discovery work with RP-05 tickets loony-fabric-bunny and pettish-snippy-rasbora.\\n- D10. Expand truncated MCP tool descriptions and regenerate the MCP reference from registrar docstrings. Keep each description client-facing and preserve schemas and contracts.\\n- D11. Repair templates/rebar-usage.md, its synchronized templates/AGENTS.md region, docs/assets/rebar-demo.svg, packaged guides, and example skills. Remove rebar-repository assumptions from portable examples or label those examples as rebar development workflows.\\n- D12. Rewrite Jira onboarding and validation documentation around implemented bridge setup, required project configuration, maintained executable paths, harness safety, current limitations, and reproduction commands.\\n- D13. Resolve governance authority and reporting-channel gaps. Add an escalation contact that is distinct from the lead maintainer route, then align SUPPORT.md, GOVERNANCE.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, SECURITY.md, and mirror operations.\\n- D14. Reduce AGENTS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, and related root policies to current contributor and agent process. Replace repeated explanations with pointers to the authoritative internal document.\\n- D15. Restrict docs/architecture.md, docs/event-schema.md, docs/concurrency.md, and docs/maintenance-audit-runbook.md to implemented architecture and current development process.\\n- D16. Remove obsolete remediation plans and completed execution records from living guidance after preserving unique history on their tickets. Correct deleted shell writer references and absent-feature claims.\\n- D17. Define required ADR lifecycle metadata and validate status, date, owner, ticket, decision relationships, implementation state, and applicability in addition to numbering and links.\\n- D18. Normalize the ADR set. Mark ADR 0042 and ADR 0090 as superseded, reduce execution transcripts and incident logs, and preserve decision, rationale, alternatives, invariants, consequences, and relationship links.\\n- D19. Promote the durable batch-runner seam from docs/design/batch-runner-seam.md into ADR 0003 or a new ADR. Move its implementation chronology to tickets.\\n- D20. Rewrite operational runbooks against effective configuration and maintained paths. Correct two-vote gate state, GitHub mirror capabilities, SSO links, and review-bot operations. Move rollout transcripts and incidents to tickets.\\n- D21. Define lifecycle and provenance metadata for research, calibration, experiments, archives, and frozen corpora. Keep procedures and reproducibility inputs separate from outcomes and production applicability.\\n- D22. Rewrite production comments and docstrings around nonobvious behavior, safety, ordering, ownership, failure semantics, concurrency, and external constraints. Move chronology to tickets or ADRs.\\n- D23. Add public API docstrings for unlink, tag, untag, archive, and compact in src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py.\\n- D24. Normalize reviewer prompts, criteria routing data, evaluation specifications, and schema descriptions without changing criteria meaning, labels, scoring intent, or machine contracts.\\n- D25. Rewrite diagnostics, logs, workflow annotations, shell output, and presentation strings while preserving error codes, field names, structured markers, compatibility tokens, and tested wording.\\n- D26. Rewrite test comments around protected invariants and failure oracles. Reduce workflow, infrastructure, configuration, and experiment comments to current operational rationale.\\n- D27. Complete third-party provenance and distribution notices. Cover the alias wordlist license, package license-files, NOTICE, the legacy wordlist header, and the vendored Jira Data Center Dockerfile revision and license.\\n- D28. Extend internal-link validation from docs to every maintained root, infra, example, template, package, and help document. Define source-aware exclusions for generated and frozen material.\\n- D29. Record canonical source ownership for every generated or synchronized artifact. Change generated output only through its source and verify regeneration in portable checks.\\n- D30. After the RP-05 registry cutover, verify that top-level help discovers explain, review-plan, review-code, verify-completion, scan-spec, and workflow without adding a competing implementation ticket.\\n\\nThis register is provisional. Every item still requires the two remaining shard reports and three independent filters. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787290251329414001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Provisional candidate register. C01 defines a documentation taxonomy and ownership policy. C02 adds context-aware punctuation, diction, and paragraph checks. C03 expands comment hygiene across maintained formats and removes citation-only historical exemptions. C04 reduces README.md to client onboarding. C05 separates client and developer paths in the documentation index. C06 corrects operation-certificate guidance around DSSE envelopes and SSHSIG. C07 corrects import idempotency, batching, push, and recovery guidance. C08 completes CLI option and command discovery while coordinating with active registry work. C09 fixes MCP summary extraction and environment metadata drift checks. C10 corrects adoption templates, demonstrations, and agent skills. C11 narrows the user guide to supported client workflows. C12 splits configuration guidance by audience and corrects stale links or future plans. C13 corrects identity setup and exempt type names. C14 marks JIRA_PROJECT as required and adds workflow preflight. C15 reduces Jira sync setup to operator actions and supported limitations. C16 replaces the plan guide with a concise workflow and verified example paths. C17 narrows support and security policies to their external purposes. C18 makes CONTRIBUTING.md canonical and reduces AGENTS.md plus the first-change guide to audience-specific constraints and pointers. C19 aligns the ChatGPT guide on validation and import troubleshooting. C20 rewrites architecture, event schema, and concurrency documentation around current Python seams. C21 repairs ADR links, statuses, supersession, and generated index metadata. C22 moves completed plans, transcripts, and implementation history to tickets or ADRs. C23 keeps exit-code documentation focused on current behavior. C24 fills public library docstring and reuse-surface gaps. C25 corrects stale Jira backend narration. C26 reduces production comments and docstrings to current rationale and invariants. C27 normalizes prompts, schemas, routing data, and evaluation specifications without changing contracts. C28 remediates diagnostics, logs, audit UI text, and demonstration output while preserving structured fields. C29 reduces workflow, infrastructure, and configuration comments to current operational rationale. C30 rewrites test comments around protected invariants while preserving wording fixtures. C31 separates experiment procedure from results and preserves immutable evidence with provenance. C32 removes ornamental dividers and comments that duplicate code after manual review. C33 refocuses MCP authentication, S3, and Gerrit setup documents on their operator audiences. C34 audits package metadata, templates, and remaining integration examples for accuracy and audience fit. Every item remains provisional until exploration and filtering finish. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787290406022862001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root verification confirmed three cross-shard findings. README.md contains Install headings at lines 26 and 197. docs/README.md describes six relations, while docs/ticket-model.md, docs/event-schema.md, and shipped link help define seven relations including caused_by. The shared documentation action checks ADR numbering, generated indexes and references, links, the README quickstart, selected vocabulary, DCO identity, conflict markers, file size, and contract tests. It does not invoke the comment hygiene checker or enforce the supplied prose and taxonomy rules.","timestamp":1787290520610197001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Coverage map at repository HEAD 8fa8f36b6482b2371128607a63c5483a9783e887.\\n\\n| Surface group | Exploration owner | Treatment | Inventory |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Root client, governance, contributor, and harness documents | Shards A and B by audience | Full factual, taxonomy, prose, and link review | 10 root documents |\\n| Top-level docs pages | Shards A and B by audience | Full review with living guidance separated from history | 65 pages |\\n| Numbered ADRs plus ADR indexes | Shard A | Decision lifecycle, metadata, relationship, accuracy, and prose review | 103 artifacts |\\n| Design, research, calibration, experiment, archive, and migration material | Shard A | Lifecycle and provenance review. Maintained procedure receives prose review | 164 experiment assets plus related records |\\n| Infrastructure modules and runbooks | Shard A for documents and Shard C for embedded comments | Current-state, path, configuration, safety, and prose review | 14 documents |\\n| Examples and templates | Shard B for client text and Shard C for embedded comments | Portability, accuracy, completeness, synchronization, and prose review | 18 documents |\\n| CLI help sources | Shard B | Full command, option, behavior, discovery, and prose review | 55 files |\\n| Packaged explain guides | Shard B | Client-audience, portability, behavior, and prose review | 3 files |\\n| MCP registrar descriptions | Shard B | Tool discovery, parameter, behavior, error, and generated-reference review | All registered tools and the generated reference |\\n| Reviewer prompts | Shard C | Maintained prompt meaning and prose review with contract preservation | 87 files |\\n| Evaluation and workflow text | Shard C | Maintained specification and prose review with oracle preservation | 40 assets |\\n| Source Python | Shard C | Tokenized comment and docstring review plus registered presentation strings | 555 files |\\n| Script files | Shard C | Comment, help, diagnostic, and output review | 66 files |\\n| Test Python | Shard C | Comment and docstring review. Wording fixtures remain protected | 1,511 files |\\n| Workflow, configuration, Terraform, and related text | Shard C for embedded prose and Shard A for standalone runbooks | Operational rationale, current state, and presentation text review | 91 files |\\n| Schemas and structured descriptions | Shard C unless client-facing | Description-field review with key, enum, and contract preservation | All maintained schemas |\\n| Machine corpora, captures, wordlists, binary assets, and generated evidence | Root provenance check | Provenance, license, source, digest, and regeneration review. No line-level rewriting of frozen content | 156 machine-corpus assets plus binary and wordlist artifacts |\\n\\nUntracked dependencies, .git state, virtual environments, caches, and build output are outside the repository inventory. Generated documents are assessed through their canonical source and regeneration contract. Third-party license text remains verbatim. External captures, frozen model output, serialized fixtures, and wording-under-test cases remain immutable evidence. Their maintained wrappers, provenance metadata, labels, and explanatory text remain in scope. Technical identifiers, command syntax, code operators, schema keys, machine markers, and table separators remain outside prose replacement rules while the prose around them remains in scope.\\n\\nShard precedence prevents double counting. Client-facing strings belong to Shard B. Comments and docstrings belong to Shard C. Standalone internal records belong to Shard A. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787290780172350001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Accuracy checkpoint. src/rebar/graph/_links.py defines seven canonical relations. docs/user-guide.md omits caused_by from its relation list, while AGENTS.md says six relations. Documentation should derive the inventory or enforce parity against CANONICAL_RELATIONS. The same check confirms that docs/config.md names the wrong ADR number for both cross-ticket overlap and transport retry. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787291091245447001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation and configuration evidence map for the provisional candidates.\\n\\n- Operation certificates. src/rebar/schemas/sign_result.schema.json and docs/migrations/hmac-opcert-removal.md establish sshsig over a DSSE envelope for plan-review and completion-verifier certificates. The maintained HMAC claims listed in the prior checkpoint conflict with that contract.\\n- Ticket relations. docs/ticket-model.md and src/rebar/_cli/help/unlink.txt establish seven relations, including caused_by, and an optional relation selector for unlink. README.md and client templates conflict.\\n- Claim identity. docs/config.md and docs/user-guide.md establish configured default assignment and Jira-resolvable explicit identities. README.md, client templates, the demo SVG, and .agents/rules/rebar.md instruct explicit placeholder or bare-handle assignment.\\n- Import behavior. src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py and docs/scale-envelope.md establish source_id skip behavior, crash resumption, deferred push, and chunk-level commits. src/rebar/_cli/help/import.txt, the generated CLI reference, and docs/import-export.md retain pre-batching claims.\\n- Jira project selection. src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py, runtime.py, and src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py require a configured project for access, inbound scope, and writes. docs/config.md, docs/jira-sync-setup.md, bridge-probe help, and generated CLI help describe a DIG fallback or call the project optional.\\n- Jira onboarding. src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py and ADR 0070 establish rebar bridge setup. scripts/jira-onboarding-reference/README.md calls the flow planned.\\n- Jira pressure tools. Both maintained pressure scripts default REBAR_TICKET_CLI to deleted src/rebar/_engine/rebar. Their README therefore describes commands that cannot start from the current checkout.\\n- Identity propagation. Four maintained workflows export REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY through GITHUB_ENV for later steps. docs/identity-setup.md says that channel does not reach later steps.\\n- CLI syntax. src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/writes.py accepts a positional parent and --detected-by for create. src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/lifecycle.py accepts --caused-by, --ref, and structured output for transition. The committed help omits part of those surfaces.\\n- MCP summaries. docs/mcp-reference.md truncates create_identity, create_ticket, link_tickets, log_session, reopen_ticket, set_file_impact, and transition_ticket at hard line breaks in registrar docstrings. The transition registrar also describes a narrower close contract than the CLI and core.\\n- Effective Gerrit gate state. infra/gerrit/project.config contains an active Verified submit requirement. infra/runbooks/two-vote-gate-rollback.md says the requirement ships inactive.\\n- GitHub mirror capabilities. SUPPORT.md uses GitHub Issues and the Verified gate uses GitHub Actions. infra/runbooks/github-mirror-lock.md instructs operators to disable both.\\n- SSO operations. infra/terraform/modules/sso-gate/README.md links to missing infra/shared/auth/RUNBOOK.md. The maintained runbook is infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md.\\n- ADR lifecycle. ADR 0042 and ADR 0090 declare Accepted after explicit supersession notices. scripts/check_adr_numbers.py checks numbering, markers, and links only.\\n- Internal architecture. docs/architecture.md includes unimplemented ADR 0098 and ADR 0100 designs as architecture sections, plus completed module-split histories. docs/concurrency.md and docs/event-schema.md name retired shell writers.\\n- Obsolete plans. docs/oss-comparison-and-remediation.md and docs/remediation-implementation-plan.md retain absent-feature claims for capabilities now present in source.\\n- Module policy. docs/maintenance-audit-runbook.md calls 800 lines a soft cap. .github/module-size-limit.txt and AGENTS.md define an absolute cap.\\n- Public library documentation. unlink, tag, untag, archive, and compact are exported from src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py without function docstrings.\\n- Prompt inventory. tests/unit/test_reviewer_prompt_hygiene.py says the glob covers 41 reviewer prompts. The current glob resolves 58 files.\\n- Generated and synchronized surfaces. docs/adr/README.md is generated, templates/AGENTS.md contains a synchronized canonical region, and CLI help files have a generator. The current generated-surface table does not catalog every such surface.\\n- Link scope. scripts/check_docs_index.py validates relative links under docs. It does not cover the broken internal link found under infra.\\n- Third-party material. pyproject.toml lists only LICENSE in license-files. The v2 alias wordlist cites docs/licenses/adjective-adjective-animal-LICENSE.txt. The legacy wordlist lacks provenance. The Jira Data Center Dockerfile names an upstream path without an upstream revision or license.\\n- Skill metadata. examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md lacks the name field required by examples/agent-skills/README.md.\\n- Help discovery. Top-level help omits six routed command families identified in the prior checkpoint. Open RP-05 tickets loony-fabric-bunny and pettish-snippy-rasbora own the registry and generated-reference cutover.\\n\\nThis map records expected behavior sources rather than scan-count inference. No project files changed.","timestamp":1787291364519298001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root verification confirmed representative internal-document placement defects. docs/README.md explains four failed CI iterations from story 316a inside current generated-artifact guidance. docs/config.md presents itself as an accepted design that implementation tasks will build toward and retains retired gate history. docs/migrations.md mixes the implemented ensure registry with a future ordered ledger and story chronology. scripts/gen_adr_index.py emits prohibited connectors and hard-wrapped index prose, so the generator is the correction source for docs/adr/README.md.","timestamp":1787291513011281001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root verification confirmed the documentation index checker boundary. scripts/check_docs_index.py checks only top-level Markdown membership in docs/README.md and file existence for relative links that remain inside docs. It does not validate anchors, repository-root targets, subdirectory index membership, audience classification, or canonical-source metadata. Its module docstring also retains held-out TDD history instead of describing current behavior.","timestamp":1787293038963115001}],"created_at":1787285414389715001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6ee28126-9032-43c5-b6e5-3827fd97ba3a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"23e8-aef8-3434-4ffa"}],"description":"","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","23e8-aef8-3434-4ffa"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0a72-1aa6-c7be-4701","ticket_type":"session_log","title":"Read-only survey of documentation taxonomy, prose, comments, accuracy, and completeness","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b6dccb1a-4b68-462f-a595-69643e6d5ce2","2780eafc-b904-4ac9-8270-475a0baadec1","f2e23692-d009-4c84-a368-a0d17cecd62b","5a6249c5-0e37-4456-afa2-7a492f5faf2a","57669ba3-3278-4ae0-9a51-43848e3cd48e","27155ca5-e665-4e48-9ed5-d7ee455100f7","cc6973bc-9d7d-4d56-934c-bf7c1a215a4c","8db973fa-e559-416b-94c4-6246e288a4b8","606dbf73-9aac-49be-afbe-388bccdd920a","b2b6340d-ab2e-450e-8b44-90d7fa802f9f","7451b6d1-5148-4396-aaf0-839b8ee2a27f","377aeef4-42dc-4194-83c5-70a03df58a39","87bfa34e-556e-4310-b565-f7c20238a36a","57a94d2b-1883-493d-9db1-4c8718004401","f51ad97a-c553-4efd-aa4a-f5a36715b0af","f6422786-a3c3-4c6f-a297-fc10545dad92","2b46994b-ead7-49cd-b8ab-34b0842ad445","ce0937f5-e457-47d8-b2d3-72962954ed2b","6e52c39e-4d93-4869-8143-130fbac14104","54f51c44-9a0d-4732-be02-585092ad14fe","5dcccc90-aba3-466d-8508-84c538d917aa","d130adee-96a1-4484-b5be-3f9c04cb7ac4","cdae6588-588a-4b37-a10f-606faf1232c7"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787293038963115002,"uuid":"69e5cd1a-232a-459d-b10a-d8214f4bc7bf"}